  "Question": "What is the value of \\(\\left(625^{\\log_5 2015}\\right)^{\\frac14}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\sqrt[4]{2015}\\)",
    "C": "\\(625\\)",
    "D": "\\(2015\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\sqrt[4]{5^{2015}}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The logarithm has base \\(5\\), so write \\(625=5^4\\) to use the same base throughout. Let \\(t=\\log_5 2015\\). By the definition of a logarithm, \\(5^t=2015\\).\n\nAll power bases are positive, so the laws of real exponents apply:\n\\[\n\\left(625^t\\right)^{1/4}\n=\\left((5^4)^t\\right)^{1/4}\n=5^{4t/4}\n=5^t\n=2015.\n\\]\nThe fourth root is the positive root, consistent with \\(2015>0\\). Thus the value is \\(\\boxed{2015}\\), choice D.",
